# Unemployment Analysis with Python

## OASIS INFOBYTE Data Science Internship

### Task 2 — Unemployment Analysis with Python

## 📌 Project Overview

This project performs Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) on unemployment data to understand regional and temporal trends in unemployment rates in India.

The analysis focuses on unemployment patterns before and after the COVID-19 pandemic.

## 🎯 Objective

The objective of this project is to analyze unemployment data and identify important trends and patterns across different regions and time periods.

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- Python
- Pandas
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
- Seaborn
- Jupyter Notebook

## 📊 Dataset

The project uses an unemployment dataset containing information about unemployment rates across different regions and time periods in India.

## 🔎 Analysis Performed

The following analysis was performed:

- Data loading and inspection
- Shape and data type checking
- Missing-value analysis
- Data cleaning and type conversion
- Region-wise average unemployment analysis
- Month-wise unemployment trends
- Time-series analysis
- Comparison of unemployment rates across regions
- Top states/regions with the highest average unemployment
- Correlation analysis
- Pre-COVID and post-COVID comparison

## 📈 Visualizations

The project includes visualizations such as:

- Unemployment rate over time
- Regional comparison
- Top 10 states/regions by average unemployment rate
- Correlation heatmap
- COVID-19 period comparison

